{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>In a flame of fire.</b> So that he become accustomed to it, lest he be alarmed when he comes to Sinai amid the fire and the lightning." "<b>From the midst of the bush.</b> One may say: because it consists entirely of thorns, and it is impossible to carve in it a symbolic figure." "<b>And the bush was not consumed.</b> A sign regarding Egypt and Israel: for the enemy is likened to fire and Israel to the bush, and just as the fire did not consume the bush, so the enemy will not be able to destroy Israel."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:55:54.994374398Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}